  "$comment": "Campaign level 30 (S4 L7-B, chapter 3): a march home. The player lands on the western beach with only the Shaper, five wardens and five settlers; the old Hearth stands empty on the northeastern plateau, sunk in a pit of black water (so a Shaper who falls on the road cannot respawn and skip the march), a long winding road away. Any unit reaching the gate stones raises it. Pursuers (tribe 1, whose camp is on an island to the south, so they can never be wiped out early) land behind the band every 60 s and chase it to the gate (spawn plus fresh raid, until the reach stage), and a band from the Oath Stone cuts the road at the ford. Stages: bring the Shaper to the gate (reach), gain fourteen followers (fromStage), cut down twenty four pursuers (kill, tribe 1; raids every 75 s from minute 10 until done), then pray at the Oath Stone (dormant until then, held by tribe 1, posted guards plus eight keepers). Not eliminateAll. Bot (hard, offsets 0 to 5, normal) wins 20900 to 22400.",
